module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_imported_name_shadowed_by_a_kernel_name

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_imported_name_shadowed_by_a_kernel_name: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_imported_name_shadowed_by_a_kernel_name" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "an imported name shadowed by a kernel name -- a MEANING FORK INSIDE THE v1 RESOLVER. A module writes `import m { Optional }`, naming a declaration m owns, and the resolver gives that bare name two different answers depending on which lookup asks. v1.compiler.infer direct_import_export_precedence_note states the overlay's order as locals > kernel > direct-selected > transitive, and v1.compiler.infer_env overlay_skips_kernel_name lists the names no import overrides (every kernel type, the container names, Unit, Optional, Present, Absent). But a declaration-field type is bound by v1.compiler.infer_env lookup_type_for through lookup_binding, which answers from the module's own env.bindings -- its declarations AND its named imports -- before lookup_binding_by_name reaches that overlay, so the field binds the IMPORTED declaration. INVALID STATE: one name, one module, one revision, two declarations, chosen by the lookup path. Nothing refuses.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5) wherever two readers take different paths. Every consumer that re-derives the binding -- the emitter for unstamped references, the bare-provider gate, any lens -- has to choose one of the two orders, and whichever it chooses disagrees with some other reader. MEASURED on gunbc#13454 (native broker 2K-b): with the emitter's unstamped-occurrence order set kernel-first, as the note reads, the typechecker refused gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls_optional_importer with `type mismatch: expected 'Coproduct(Optional)', got 'Primitive(Int)'` at its `held: Optional<Int>` payload (head 57551c4b), proving the field had bound the imported coproduct.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the name is one overlay_skips_kernel_name admits; the module imports it BY NAME from a module that declares it; the module does not declare it itself. A module's own declaration of the leaf is not this class (both paths agree locals win). FOUND 2026-10-06 on gunbc#13454; operator ruling via gentle-dove-36: the emitter follows the binding the typechecker actually uses, so v1.compiler.infer_env bare_occurrence_binding mirrors lookup_binding (own file, then named import, then kernel) as a counted route.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor -- silent, unrefused. The pinning control is gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls_optional_importer (cases optional_imported_coproduct_*), which goes red if the emitter's order is reverted to kernel-first. The v2 resolver already refuses the Int instance of this collision (v2.compiler.resolve resolve_atom; v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation bla_imported_user_int_refuses_rather_than_binding_the_kernel_int). ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the collision is decidable at the import, from the import's selected declaration and the kernel name set. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, ONE RULE at capability grain: the v1 resolver REFUSES, at the import, every named import of a name overlay_skips_kernel_name admits when the selected declaration is not the one the kernel name denotes, so the two lookup orders can no longer disagree because the state they disagree about is unwritable. When it lands the importer fixture is rewritten as that refusal's discriminating red.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "direct_import_export_precedence_note", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "overlay_skips_kernel_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "lookup_binding", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "bare_occurrence_binding", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls_optional_importer", decl_name: "HeldChoice", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_imported_user_int_refuses_rather_than_binding_the_kernel_int", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
